sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-005: Password Recovery for PART/ADMIN — Reset Confirmation Sequence
    actor User
    participant UI as React Reset Form
    participant API as Express Auth API
    participant Firebase as Firebase Auth + Identity Toolkit
    participant DB as Supabase PostgreSQL

    User->>UI: Submit new password and confirmation for validated link
    UI->>UI: Enforce 8+ characters, upper/lowercase, digit, special character, match
    alt Client validation fails
        UI-->>User: Field errors, no reset request
    else Client validation passes
        UI->>API: POST /api/auth/password-reset/confirm
        API->>API: Revalidate action code and password policy
        alt Link changed state or password is invalid
            API-->>UI: Expired/invalid/used/OAuth/field error
            UI-->>User: Preserve appropriate state and recovery guidance
        else Confirmation is valid
            API->>Firebase: Consume action code and replace password
            Firebase-->>API: Password updated, no sign-in/session
            API->>API: Record consumed-code hash for explicit local replay state
            API->>Firebase: Remove prior mfa_auth_time claim
            API->>DB: Invalidate pending MFA challenges, retain attempts/lock
            API->>Firebase: Revoke all refresh tokens across devices
            alt Revocation fails after password change
                Firebase--xAPI: Revocation unavailable
                API-->>UI: 502 REVOCATION_FAILED, clear local cookies
                UI-->>User: Password changed but sessions may remain, show support/retry guidance
            else Revocation succeeds
                API-->>UI: 200 signedIn=false, sessionIssued=false, requiresMfa=true
                UI->>Firebase: Sign out local Firebase state
                UI-->>User: Continue to sign in with new password
                Note over User,Firebase: The next sign-in must complete US-004 email OTP before protected access.
            end
        end
    end

    Note over API,DB: MFA attempt history is retained, so password recovery does not clear an OTP lock.

